SUMMARY:Decisions\, Decisions\, Decisions! Parent Spiritual Chat
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Spiritual Experiences Group\n**Recognizing the 
 Difference Between My Will\, My Child’s Will\, and Divine Guidance**\n\n
 Is it sometimes difficult to know what decision is right\nfor everyone in 
 the family?\n\nDo you have stories of ways you’ve found to balance\nyour
  children’s rights and your own?\n\nAre you looking for tools to balance
  your inner guidance\nwith your child’s spiritual freedom?\n\n**You are 
 warmly invited to come share your stories!**\n\n“Raising a family is tru
 ly a testing ground for parents. They want to do what’s right for everyo
 ne in the family\, including themselves. Where to start?”\n—Harold Kle
 mp\, *A Modern Prophet Answers your*\n*Key Questions about Life\,* Book 3\
 , p. 63\n\n***Explore. . .***\n\n* What it means to have spiritual freedom
  for yourself and your family\n* How I can be clearly focused on divine wi
 ll when my child and I have different opinions\n* Balancing children’s r
 ights and spiritual freedom\, with the rules and structure needed at home\
 n\n**Are you looking for ways to bring more spirituality**\n**into your li
 fe and the life of your family?**\n\nWe will be sharing experiences of bei
 ng a parent and acknowledging and recognizing our own inner knowing.\nIt i
 s exciting to share stories and experiences with like-minded parents. By s
 haring\, our own inner wisdom can be strengthened and validated.\n\nParent
  discussions offer family-friendly tools in a relaxed setting for explorin
 g spiritual truths and how we live them.\nYou're warmly invited to share s
 piritual insights\, stories\, and experiences\, ask questions\, or simply 
 listen.\n**Parents\, grandparents\, and friends are always welcome.**\n\nC
 lick **[HERE](http://www.eckankar.org/explore/parents-families/)** to lear
 n about spiritual opportunities for parents and families\n\nClick **[HERE]
 (https://www.adventuresineckparenting.org/se-1/)** t﻿o read about a way 
 to fill yourself with love that may help you make family decisions
